From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-lenovo-asphalt: disable unsupported QCE

Linux 7.3 marks CRYPTO_DEV_QCE as BROKEN: the driver cannot arbitrate
access with the secure world and is slower than the CPU. No driver binds
the SoC crypto node, yet it defaults to enabled and is an interconnect
consumer, so fw_devlink keeps the aggre2_noc/mc_virt interconnect
providers sync_state() pending for the whole boot and their boot-time
bandwidth floors are never dropped. Disable this Linux consumer on the
board; leave the remote-controlled BAM and secure-world ownership
untouched. CPU crypto remains available. Do not override BROKEN.

This mirrors the Xiaomi Aurora (SM8650) board change.

Reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc6/drivers/crypto/Kconfig

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-asphalt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-asphalt.dts
@@ -446,6 +446,10 @@
 
 &qupv3_id_0 {
 	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&crypto {
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &gpu {
